  "description": "New front wall & timber fence to be made inline with neighbouring properties ",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [insert plan numbers/documents].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed replacement of the house's existing front boundary wall, fence, hedgerow and pedestrian gate with a front low wall, palisade fence and two palisade gates, and repaving of the house's front garden, would be harmful to the character and appearance of the house and Bedford Park Conservation Area, by reason of its effect on the historic accuracy and variation of the streetscene and protection of Bedford Park Conservation Area's garden suburb features, urban greening and biodiversity objectives and prevention of surface water flooding and runoff onto the public highway network, contrary to London Plan Policies HC1 and SI13, Local Plan Policies CC7, CC1, CC2, CC4 and EQ3 and the Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD.  "
